# discovery's imports (core/modules/discovery/README.md "Routes"): a CSV of made-up LinkedIn profile
# URLs uploaded and validated, the workspace's imports, one import, and its run in the worker. The
# upload's answer has the job's id: put it in http-client.private.env.json as `importJobId` for the
# last two requests. `pnpm http:run` sends a body as written and does not read a `< file` line: run
# the upload from the REST Client or the HTTP Client. The run answers 202 with the job, running; a
# second run answers 409 import_not_runnable, and GET …/imports/{job} gives the counts as it goes.

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/discovery/imports: uploads a CSV and answers the job with its validation report
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/discovery/imports
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WhytideImportBoundary
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

--WhytideImportBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="alpha-p5-030-sample.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./fixtures/alpha-p5-030-sample.csv
--WhytideImportBoundary--

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/discovery/imports: the workspace's imports, the newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/discovery/imports
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/discovery/imports/{job}: one import, its report and its run's counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/discovery/imports/{{importJobId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/discovery/imports/{job}/run: starts the validated job's run in the worker and answers the job, running
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/discovery/imports/{{importJobId}}/run
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
